Cable views adapt the following from cab-stu by formless63, commit
6bbf79655deb572df9f11490ca38e4f739ce71fb, licensed MIT by its copyright holder for
reuse here (retained in packages/section-layout/src and packages/wire-geometry/src):
- packages/layout/src/end-face.ts: end-face chirality (the end not drawn is the
  drawing mirrored about the vertical axis, rings read the other way, rotation is a
  viewing input), terminal placement, and the rule that an unknown viewed-from end
  has no face; adapted in end-face.ts.
- packages/render-svg/src/cross-section.ts: the vocabulary of drawing shield
  constructions (braid, spiral, tape, foil) as distinct explicit-geometry textures;
  re-expressed in appearance.ts and render.ts with material, finish and unknown-value rules.
The formboard and build-sheet views (packages/harness-views) are written for Specmate's
records using only the behavior of cab-stu's drawing and build sheets (stage structure,
deterministic self-contained output); no code, sheet format, artwork or font is copied.
The cable side view (packages/section-layout/src/side-view.ts) is written for Specmate's
stock and end preparation records using only the behavior of cab-stu's cable cutaway
(packages/docs/src/drawing/cutaway.ts: layers stepped out of one another and called out)
and bench strip figure (packages/docs/src/bench/figures.ts: an end as it leaves the jacket);
no code, artwork, marking, font or color table is copied.
The 3D explode and x-ray controls (packages/wire-geometry/src/explode.ts) are written for Specmate's
wire model using only the behavior of cab-stu's 3D wire view (packages/layout/src/wire-model.ts and
packages/editor-react/src/wire-scene.ts: layers pulled apart radially or axially, outer layers drawn
translucent without depth writes); no code, tuning constants or artwork is copied.
The 3D viewer's camera framing and studio lighting (packages/wire-geometry/src/framing.ts and
frontend/src/features/wire-stock/WireViewport.tsx) and its braid and strand surface shading
(packages/wire-geometry/src/materials.ts) adapt cab-stu packages/editor-react/src/model-scene.ts
(frameBox: every box corner fitted to both fields of view; makeLights: hemisphere, key, fill and
rim lights) and packages/editor-react/src/wire-scene.ts (screenTexture: round-strand crowns and
over-under braid carriers, also used as a bump map), with some light tuning values retained.
No predecessor catalog data, real designs, fonts, vendor art or comments are included.

